{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0009767","label":"oculocerebral hypopigmentation syndrome, Cross type","definition":"Oculocerebral hypopigmentation syndrome, Cross type is a rare congenital syndrome characterized by cutaneous and ocular hypopigmentation, various ocular anomalies (e.g. corneal and lens opacity, spastic ectropium, and/or nystagmus), growth deficiency, intellectual deficit and other progressive neurologic anomalies such as spastic tetraplegia, hyperreflexia, and/or athetoid movements. The clinical picture varies among patients and may also include other anomalies such as urinary tract abnormalities, Dandy-Walker malformations, and/or bilateral inguinal hernia.","synonyms":["Cross syndrome","Kramer syndrome","Oculocerebral Syndrome with Hypopigmentation","hypopigmentation oculocerebral syndrome Cross type","oculocerebral hypopigmentation syndrome"],"xrefs":["GARD:0000105","ICD9:759.89","MEDGEN:423639","OMIM:257800","Orphanet:2719","SCTID:17827007","UMLS:C2936910"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":0,"n_phenotypes":47,"mechanism_classes":[{"key":"amino_organic_acid","label":"amino acid / organic acid metabolism","via":"MONDO:0019189","via_label":"inborn disorder of amino acid and other organic acid metabolism"}]},"genes":[],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":"e_4f9f0bda10af","source":"MONDO:0009767","target":"HP:0000963","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:2719 · ORPHA:2719","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/2719","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"Oculocerebral hypopigmentation syndrome, Cross type: Thin skin (frequency HP:0040281) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:2719","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/2719","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"Thin skin — Very frequent (99-80%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.9,"